# Release Notes for version 1.5

## Major changes

### 1. CFA NetCDF Remote support
 - CFA NetCDF files can be converted to remote form in place by rewriting fragment URIs.
 - Remote CFA files can be generated alongside remote Kerchunk products.
 - Remote CFA-compatible output uses revised paths and naming conventions.
 - The implementation detects whether source data is NetCDF4-compatible before applying the remote CFA workflow.
 - 'remote' and 'sub' CLI options now impact CFA remote files.

### 2. SHEPARD Overhaul
 - Discovery of new groups as CSVs or manifest files has been improved.
 - Complete workflow of all pipeline phases, plus qurantining and deletion fully tested.
 - Bug fixes when transferring and instantiating groups via SHEPARD.
 - CLI command has been changed to `shepard`

### 3. Completion workflow
 - Now a central part of the SHEPARD workflow to complete projects and apply remote parameters.
 - Configurable version separator can now be applied.

### 4. New Features in general
 - Added support for creating repeats from a set of project codes, as well as using phase/status selection.
 - Added `aggregation_date` parameter as standard to all Kerchunk and CFA output products.

### 5. Various bug fixes
 - Memory leaks patched when running with validation, for both kerchunk and CFA
 - Issues with CFA scan failures now allowed to proceed without CFA
 - Fixed an issue with running subsets of specific project codes in parallel outside a repeat.
 - Experimental Icechunk support - fully operational in future update.
 